<figure class="cache-figure" data-layered-freshness>
 <p class="figure-title">A new local TTL must not make an old observation young</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>L1 fill time <input data-fill type="range" min="0" max="59" value="55" /><output data-fill-label>55 s</output></label><label>Local TTL <input data-ttl type="range" min="5" max="60" value="30" /><output data-ttl-label>30 s</output></label><label>Inspect at <input data-now type="range" min="0" max="120" value="75" /><output data-now-label>75 s</output></label><label><input data-enforce type="checkbox" /> Enforce the original freshness deadline</label></div>
 <div class="restore-timelines"><div><span>Original observation · valid until 60 s</span><div class="restore-track"><i style="width:50%"></i><b data-marker></b></div></div><div><span>Local copy · <span data-local-label></span></span><div class="restore-track layered-local-track"><i data-local></i><b data-marker></b></div></div><div class="restore-axis"><span>0 s · source observed</span><span>120 s</span></div></div>
 <p class="cluster-command" data-decision></p><p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>The L2 value carries an observation made at 0 s and a freshness deadline of 60 s. L1 receives that same observation later. Both bars use one time scale; the marker is the inspection time. No invalidation arrives during the model. The optional check enforces application metadata bound to the value, not an automatic feature of a local cache’s TTL.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{localDeadline}from'../../lib/caching/tracking.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-layered-freshness]').forEach(root=>{const fill=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fill]')!,ttl=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-ttl]')!,now=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-now]')!,enforce=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-enforce]')!;const render=()=>{const s=localDeadline(Number(fill.value),Number(ttl.value),enforce.checked,Number(now.value));for(const key of['fill','ttl','now']as const)root.querySelector(`[data-${key}-label]`)!.textContent=`${s[key]} s`;const bar=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-local]')!;bar.style.marginLeft=`${s.fill/120*100}%`;bar.style.width=`${(s.end-s.fill)/120*100}%`;root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-marker]').forEach(m=>m.style.left=`${s.now/120*100}%`);root.querySelector('[data-local-label]')!.textContent=`${s.fill} s → ${s.end} s`;root.querySelector('[data-decision]')!.textContent=s.now<s.fill?'L1 has not received the copy yet':s.accepted?'L1 returns the cached observation':'L1 must reload or decline the answer';root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=enforce.checked?`The local deadline is min(${s.fill} + ${s.ttl}, 60) = ${s.end} s. Copying the value cannot extend the original contract.`:s.accepted&&s.tooOld?`The local TTL permits a hit at ${s.now} s, but the original observation is already beyond its 60 s limit. Starting a new timer extended its apparent validity to ${s.local} s.`:`The new local timer ends at ${s.local} s. The original source observation still dates from 0 s; a new location does not reset its age.`;};for(const input of[fill,ttl,now])input.oninput=render;enforce.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
